# Commit convention

Owner: INV-COMMIT-01 in `.context-circuit/wrapper/contracts/invariants.yaml`.
This file restates the no-attribution clause because a worker, a host git
wrapper, or any path that does not open the invariant still commits. It does
not replace the owner.

## Shape

`type(scope): imperative subject` — lowercase type (`feat`, `fix`, `docs`,
`refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`), optional scope,
no trailing period. An optional body explains why. No credentials, provider
payloads, or host-specific paths.

## No attribution (absolute)

Never add an AI attribution, credit, co-author, or "generated by" footer or
trailer to a commit, pull request, merge request, review, or comment. The
human is the sole recorded author.

Forbidden, without limitation:

- `Co-authored-by` / `Co-Authored-By` naming an assistant or bot (Claude,
  Codex, Cursor, or similar)
- `Generated with` / `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code]`
- `Made with Cursor` / `Made-with: Cursor`
- `Claude-Session` or any equivalent credit to a tool, model, provider, or
  this agent

## Host injection

Claude Code `attribution`, Codex `commit_attribution`, and Cursor Attribution
inject trailers after `git commit`. Disable them. Do not re-add them.

After every commit you authored, inspect the recorded message
(`git log -1 --format='%B'`). If a forbidden trailer is present, rewrite that
recorded message so it is gone before you finish. Do not leave it on the
branch.

This restates INV-COMMIT-01.
